UID:123122-1791883800-1791894600@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:STEAM Career Showcase for Students with Disabilities
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 13th annual STEAM Career Showcase for Students with Disabilities – a free event for learners in grades 6–12. Connect with role models with disabilities who have thriving careers in the fields of Science\, Technology\, Engineering\, Arts\, and Math (STEAM). Learn about their personal journeys and strategies for success. Gain practical knowledge that you can apply to your interests and future career paths. \nASL interpretation and live captions will be provided for welcome\, keynote presentation\, and panel discussion. Registration closes on Friday\, October 9th. \nRegister Now \n  \n\nSchedule\n9:30am: Doors Open & Check In \n10:00am: Welcome \n10:15am: Keynote Presentation with Q&A \n11:00am – 12:30 pm: Opportunity Fair with Exhibitors \nNoon – 12:30pm: Panel Discussion \n\nKeynote Speaker\n \nDr. Louis Vaught\nPostdoctoral Research Associate in Chemical and Mechanical Engineering at The University of Tulsa \nAn engineer who develops new materials and manufacturing technologies\, Dr. Vaught has worked on some exciting projects. These include wearable batteries woven into clothing\, plastics that survive harsh environments like the North Pole\, and even reusable glue for building satellites in orbit.\n\n\nPanelists\n \nTrusha Patel\nPhysical Therapy Student at Campbell University \n\nTrusha aims to help people get back to the things they love doing after an injury\, illness or life-changing event. As an amputee and future physical therapist\, her personal experience inspired her passion for rehabilitation and helping others.\n\n\n–\n\n\nLacey Roy\nNeurosociology Student at UNC Chapel Hill \n\n\nA non-traditional student at UNC-Chapel Hill\, Lacey has her heart set on a career in neurosociology\, thanks to her curiosity about how humans “work”. In one of her research projects\, she studies specific ways stigma is perpetuated against the deaf community.\n\n–\n\n\nVictorial Covell \nDesigner\, Performer & Accessibility Advocate\n–\n\nA graduate of The Rochester Institute of Technology\, Victoria has 25+ years of performance arts experience and has designed creative for organizations including NASA and Blumenthal Performing Arts. With the NC Division of Services for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing\, she travels to lead interactive theatre improv workshops for students.\n\n\n\nExhibitors\n\nNCMNS Teen Programs\nFind out about programs & volunteer opportunities for middle and high school students\, right here at the Museum.\n–\nCatalyst at NC State\nGet information about the free\, award-winning program that prepares high school students with disabilities for careers in STEM fields.\n–\nAutism Society of North Carolina\nSpeak with an employment specialist from ASNC who helps autistic job seekers in their search.\n–\nYouth LEAD NC\nLearn about the NC Youth Leadership Forum on NC State’s campus\, where participants get an on-site college experience before even graduating from high school.\n–\nNC ABLE Program\nGain knowledge about financial resources for people with disabilities\, including savings accounts and investments.\n\n–\nLibrary of NC’s Accessible Books and Library Services\nLearn how print disabilities make standard print inaccessible and how they help remove barriers through free audiobooks\, braille\, large print\, accessible technology and personalized support.\n–\n\nNorth Carolina State Laboratory of Public Health\nLook through mini portable microscopes to view microscopic images of everyday things\, and try to identify them. Use real tools used by scientists!\n\n–\nMeet the Animals\nGet up close and personal with some of the Museum’s live specimens\, or we call them\, animal ambassadors.\n\n–\n\n\nVirtual Option\nFor those unable to join in person\, the welcome and keynote speeches will be livestreamed on the Museum’s YouTube channel.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/steam-career-showcase-2026/
LOCATION:Nature Exploration Center\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Accessible,K-12 Students,Youth Science Program
ORGANIZER;CN="Samantha%20Frigerio":MAILTO:Samantha.Frigerio@naturalsciences.org
